# Local Intent Guard state (contracts and runtime files belong in consuming app
# repos). This repo ignores the whole directory; a consuming repo should commit
# it and ignore only .intent-guard/drift-log.jsonl. The legacy name is kept here
# so a working copy that has not been migrated yet stays untracked.
.intent-guard/
.conductor/
.cursor/
# The umbrella's hook manifest, under .guardrails, records absolute paths on
# whichever machine installed the hook, so it stays local. The policy file
# beside it, .guardrails.yaml, is tracked: CI reads it.
.guardrails/
# Maintainer records. The public content policy already says these must not be
# committed: maintainer status, week-ahead plans, and dogfood validation notes.
# They were tracked anyway until 2026-09-04, so this is the rule catching up
# with the repository. They stay on disk; they just stop being published.
BRAINSTORMING.md
